From 8fce8b7d2a3d03f7b054abdc0413f87a1ce2ce78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:08:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Don't keep the server fallback if the content spawned a
 deferred render

If the client render suspends only on the initial value of
useDeferredValue, the deferred render has to re-enter the primary children.
Only the regular fallback path schedules it, via
getRemainingWorkInPrimaryTree, so use that path in this case. Otherwise the
deferred lane was dropped and the content stayed hidden behind the server
fallback, retrying in a loop.

Also fold the regression test for #37620 into ReactDOMFizzServer-test next to
the other browser() tests, including the check that the server fallback node
is never removed while the content is suspended.
